      ":question/problem": "![](images/28/28f56656e191e342a4815ba74bdd29cba5247fba7d8ab0feca8ffbe0b785ab8c.png)\n\nConsider a sample of size $n = 100$ from a population with standard deviation $\u03c3 = 5$. Given that the mean of the sample is $x^(\u2015) = 14$, find a $95%$ confidence interval for the population mean $\u03bc$ of the distribution.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $P(Z > 1.96) = 0.025$, where $Z\u223cN(0, 1)$, as shown in the diagram above.*\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
